## Cycle 142 frontier-family screen log (22 October 2026)

**Why this entry exists, and why it is written now rather than in Cycle 142.** Cycle 142's Priority 1 produced the
register's **first frontier inventory** — a bounded list of **16 entries** of published state kinds the register had
not screened — and its Priority 2 screened exactly one of them (entry 8, an ESG/sustainability fund classification),
which was **killed by G-12** and logged as **R-072**. Cycle 142's pre-registration required that "a one-paragraph
summary of this inventory" be written into this register "**beside the frontier-family screen log**", and six
artifacts state that it "is recorded in `research/idea_register.md` beside the frontier-family screen log".
**That claim was false as written.** The summary paragraph was written into the register's **header block**,
immediately below the "Last updated: **Cycle 142 complete**" line, and **this screen-log series carried no
Cycle-142 entry at all** — it ran from "## Cycle 13 frontier-family screen log" to "## Cycles 67–94
frontier-family screen log" and stopped there. A reader consulting the register's cumulative family-screen record
would not have found the inventory's summary anywhere in it. **The entry below is the placement the Cycle-142
pre-registration asked for; it is additive, and the header-block copy is retained.**

**The summary itself.** The register's first frontier inventory lists **16 published state kinds it has not
screened**, written into `cycle_notes.md` as a method-level document (within the twelve-to-twenty-five bound) and
seeded from the canonical prompt's own family list. Each entry states the kind, the adjacent closed map rows it
touches, and one of four recorded reasons for not having been screened — **(i)** not a kind of published
institutional object at all (a constructed index, a vendor score, a private or model-internal quantity);
**(ii)** a member of an already-closed map row; **(iii)** never named by the register in any artifact; **(iv)** named
by the register in an artifact but never screened — plus **one explicit exclusion** (the combinations family, which
the register's own rule excludes). Every entry was checked against the **34 coverage-map rows** and the **111
known-baseline rows** for non-duplication.

**Two are constructed measures, not published state kinds** (reason (i)): **trend and momentum** and
**cross-sectional effects**, which duplicate published baselines **1, 3, 39** and **1, 2, 9, 40** respectively.

**One remains a genuine gap never named by the register in any artifact** (reason (iii)): **bank stress-test /
capital-plan outcome** (entry 7). **Three more are reason-(iv) entries** — named by the register in an artifact and
screened, with a never-named residual: **portfolio construction** (entry 3; residual: a non-index allocation
mandate — a fund's or a pension scheme's published concentration cap or glide path); **mutual-fund flow / AUM
state** (entry 9; residual: an industry body's monthly fund-flow report read as a decision-time state);
**crypto staking / unstaking schedule or lockup** (entry 10; residual: the protocol staking rule — lockup,
unbonding or slashing conditions). **The four that remain standing**
are recorded, with their adjacent closed rows, in `cycle_notes.md`'s Cycle-143 record and are **available to a
future cycle's Priority 2** under the unchanged admission form at zero fetches; **entry 11 was screened and killed
in Cycle 145 (R-074), and the admission form's newness statement is now made against the reference set of forty-nine named
constructions** (forty-six before Cycle 142, plus the one Cycle 142 itself added, plus the one Cycle 144 added —
R-073 — the sovereign credit rating / watchlist action, inventory entry 6, which was taken and screened in Cycle
144 and killed, plus the one Cycle 145 added — R-074 — the published securitization / ABS pool performance report,
inventory entry 11, which was taken and screened in Cycle 145 and killed). **Cycle-145 correction (before → after),
made in place.** The sentence this replaces read "**Five remain genuine gaps never named by the register in any
artifact** (reason (iii)): **portfolio construction** (entry 3); **bank stress-test / capital-plan outcome**
(entry 7); **mutual-fund flow / AUM state** (entry 9); **crypto staking / unstaking schedule or lockup**
(entry 10); **published securitization / ABS pool performance report** (entry 11). **The five that remain standing**". **That
sentence was false in three respects**, and the defect was found by the Cycle-145 register-memory audit over the five
standing entries at zero fetches: the kinds of entries 3, 9 and 10 had been named by the register in artifacts and
screened (entry 3 by **R-022**, **X-1 probe P18**, **S-246** and **S-138**; entry 9 by **S-040**, **S-024**,
**S-292** and known-baseline **row 78**; entry 10 by **S-170**, **R-014**, known-baseline **row 45** and **R-028**),
so each is a reason **(iv)** entry. **Before → after:** "**Five remain genuine gaps never named by the register in
any artifact** (reason (iii))" → "**One remains a genuine gap never named by the register in any artifact**
(reason (iii)): **bank stress-test / capital-plan outcome** (entry 7) **and three more are reason-(iv) entries**". **Cycle-144 correction (before → after), made in place.** The sentence this replaces read "**Seven
are genuine gaps never named by the register in any artifact** (reason (iii)): portfolio construction (entry 3);
