**Six duplicate closed map rows or published baselines** (reason (ii)): **central-bank policy rate** → row A /
baseline 68; **central-bank balance-sheet composition** → row 13; **exchange trading-halt / circuit-breaker
state** → row 19; **exchange maintenance-margin schedule** → row 19 / baseline 32; **published corporate-action
record** → row 10 / baseline 54; **economic data release calendar** → row 10. **The combinations family** is
recorded as an explicit exclusion, not as a gap.

**The inventory fetches nothing, cites nothing, reads no ledger entry, screens nothing and mints no identifier.**
Its value is that it makes the register's coverage **auditable** for the first time: the register can now state
which published state kinds it has not examined. **It does not answer the register's binding constraint** — the
supply of constructions — and it is not reported as if it did. **Completeness is not verifiable from the register's
own artifacts**, so the inventory is a lower bound on the register's uncovered space in the same sense that the
coverage map is a lower bound on its covered space.

